WEBVTT

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.756
Fire.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.136
The asteroid is fragmenting,
but most of the debris

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.367
is still on a collision course
with the planet.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.807
Target the fragments.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.104
Destroy them.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.668
That asteroid
should have been vaporized.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.701
What happened?

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.407
I'm not sure.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.848
Sensors showed a simple
nickel-iron composition.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.112
We shouldn't be seeing fragments

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.551
more than a centimeter
in diameter.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.520
Ambassador,
I'm afraid I was right.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.455
This isn't going to work.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.219
The same thing happened
to us yesterday.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.159
We tried to vaporize
two incoming asteroids,

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.128
but they fragmented
and struck the surface.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.131
I've destroyed
most of the debris, Captain.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.757
However, targeting scanners

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.791
were unable to track
two of the fragments.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.167
They have already entered
the upper atmosphere.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.949
The debris impacted
on the largest continent

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.454
approximately 500 kilometers

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.888
from the southern tip.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.414
The central desert.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:16.292
Fortunately, that region
isn't heavily populated.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.921
Substantial cratering,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.159
atmospheric shock waves...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.633
and large concentrations of dust

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.329
and other
stratospheric contaminants.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.837
How long
until the next asteroid hits?

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.305
Approximately six hours.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.865
Can you give us an idea
of its trajectory?

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.139
Same continent, but this time
on the eastern coastal region.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.876
Our largest colonies are there.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.850
Over 5,000 citizens.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:42.719
Captain, we appreciate
your efforts,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.985
but I think it's time
we considered an evacuation.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.150
According to my analysis,

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.183
there are at least
12 more asteroids heading

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.195
in our direction.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.696
How can we hope
to destroy them all

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.697
even with your help?

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.221
Incoming hail from the surface.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.461
It's coming from one
of the heavily damaged areas.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.867
On screen.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:00.168
Ambassador,
I've been analyzing the debris

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.265
and I've discovered
disturbing evidence

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.833
that the asteroids
are not what they seem.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.040
They are composed
of artificial materials.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.946
I must meet
with you immediately.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.416
I think we can stop...

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.214
I've lost the transmission.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.050
Location?

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.146
I can't find them.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.520
Too much interference.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.888
That was Dr. Vatm,

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.916
our most prominent
astrophysicist.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.895
He mentioned the composition
of the asteroids.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.795
Could he have found
something important?

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.958
At this point, Ambassador,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.900
I don't know
what that discovery could be.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:32.063
Mr. Paris, can we send a shuttle
down through that turbulence?

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.768
It would be a rough ride,
but I think it's possible.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.708
Our chances of finding
Dr. Vatm are slim.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.870
We should evacuate the colonies.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.573
We haven't time to evacuate
all those people.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.741
I won't give up, not now.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:49.988
Captain, I'm asking
for your help again...

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.614
but I won't ask you
to risk your crew.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.991
In for a penny, in for a pound.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.460
Excuse me?

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.090
It's a human expression,
Ambassador.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:02.101
And it means
we're not leaving you now.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.762
Tuvok, assemble rescue teams.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:06.397
We'll send down
three shuttles to find Dr. Vatm.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.406
Aye, Captain.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.429
Mr. Paris?

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.368
Bridge to Engineering.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.776
B'Elanna, I want you
to beam aboard

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.178
a sample of the debris
from that last asteroid.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.114
Let's find out
why it wasn't vaporized.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.209
I'm going to study the data
we've collected so far.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.651
I'll be in my ready room.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.951
I need analeptic compounds.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.757
Are you ill?

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.526
No, no!
I'm feeling quite vigorous.

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.624
I requested a place
on the rescue team

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.134
as part of my Starfleet training

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.363
and the Captain said yes.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.665
So, I thought
it might be useful

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.536
to bring along a few
extra medical supplies.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.973
We have some analeptic compounds
in the bio lab.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.236
I'll get them for you.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.950
May I suggest a tranquilizer?

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.319
No, no, no.
I'll be fine.

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.915
Just that I'm
a little apprehensive.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.983
I've been assigned
to Lieutenant Tuvok's team,

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:03.825
and no matter what I do,
I can't seem to please him.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.331
Vulcans are notoriously
difficult to impress.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:09.164
Mr. Tuvok seldom
acknowledges my brilliance.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.897
A word of advice, Mr. Neelix.

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:14.395
Try to restrain
your... enthusiasm.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.567
You're there
to observe and learn.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:19.372
Yeah.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.470
It's good advice, Doctor.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.952
Altitude: 15 kilometers.

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:32.287
Velocity: Mach 2.1.

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:37.228
Entering the upper troposphere.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.895
Mr. Sklar,
are you all right?

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:43.959
I'm an exo-geologist.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:46.061
I prefer working on the ground.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.504
We'll be landing shortly.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.132
Try to relax.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.665
Ah!

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.541
What's happening?!

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.978
We're entering a layer
of electrodynamic turbulence.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.708
Full power to thrusters.

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:58.910
Thrusters aren't responding.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.976
Attempting to level our descent.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.787
Oh, oh!

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.849
We're losing main power!

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.884
I will have to land
the shuttle manually.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.156
Brace for impact.

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:13.926
Commander, I've lost contact
with Tuvok's shuttle.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.557
Hail them.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.330
No response.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.668
Notify Lieutenant Paris
and the others.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.070
We may have a team down.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.074
Torres to Bridge.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:23.598
Go ahead.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.907
We've beamed aboard
a piece of the debris.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.674
I'll be right there.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:28.805
Ambassador?

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:01.777
Dr. Vatm.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.009
I heard what sounded
like a ship crashing.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.541
I came looking for you.

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:07.917
This is Hanjuan.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.386
He's a miner at the nearby
gallicite excavation.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.118
He heard your ship, too.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.149
Have you seen any other
vessels like ours?

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.251
No. Just you.

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:16.522
Doctor, you said
you had information

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:17.790
on the composition
of the asteroids.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.797
What is it?

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.321
That data is classified.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.493
I can only speak
to the ambassador.

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.025
You may also speak to me.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.901
Your ambassador sent us
to find you.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.599
No.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.232
I prefer to wait.

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:31.505
Doctor, we almost died
trying to get that information.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:32.511
Tell us.

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:33.512
Be silent, Sklar!

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:35.514
Now, gentlemen,
there's no point in arguing.

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.607
Right now, we have to get
this shuttle off the ground.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.948
Unfortunately,
that will not be possible.

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:42.147
All primary systems
are off-line.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:44.315
Warp drive and impulse engines
have been destroyed.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.291
I suggest we repair
the com system

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:47.849
and send a distress call.

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:49.862
How long will that take?

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.158
Several hours, at least.

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.255
We don't have several hours.

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.265
When the next asteroid hits,

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.732
it could destroy
this entire region.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.166
We've got to get
out of here soon.

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:58.500
I assure you, we're doing
everything we can.

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.733
Mr. Neelix, please go outside

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:02.638
and inspect
the toroidal antenna.

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.644
I need to know if any of the
signal relays were damaged.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.509
If they were,
I can try to repair them.

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:08.673
A damage report
will be sufficient.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:12.213
I've been studying
with Lieutenant Torres.

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:15.482
She gave me a full orientation
on shuttlecraft systems.

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:16.510
The damage report, Mr. Neelix.

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:18.724
Aye, sir.

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:20.555
In the meantime,

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:23.426
I suggest everyone
try to remain calm.

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:24.827
Allowing anxiety to overcome you

00:09:24.864 --> 00:09:28.459
will only hinder
the efficiency of our efforts.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.560
He's really
a very pleasant fellow

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:31.797
once you get to know him.

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:32.861
And intelligent.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:34.702
I'm sure he'll have the com
system up and running...

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.707
Neelix.

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:37.743
On my way.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.226
Why won't you share the data?

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:05.395
Excuse me.
Mr. Tuvok?

00:10:05.437 --> 00:10:06.961
You couldn't have
finished already.

00:10:07.038 --> 00:10:08.198
Not exactly.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:11.607
What I mean to say is,
I know I'm here to observe

00:10:11.643 --> 00:10:13.440
and I don't mean
to step out of line,

00:10:13.478 --> 00:10:16.675
but I think I've observed
a way out of here.

00:10:16.715 --> 00:10:18.205
Where?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.808
I saw what appeared to be

00:10:19.851 --> 00:10:22.081
an orbital tether
anchored nearby.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.985
Yes, we use those
to lift cargo from the surface

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:25.181
to the orbital supply stations.

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:27.987
May I assume it uses
magnetic leverage

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:29.185
to lift the carriage?

00:10:29.227 --> 00:10:30.194
Yes.

00:10:30.228 --> 00:10:31.286
What is your point?

00:10:32.831 --> 00:10:35.527
What if we use that carriage
to climb the tether?

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:37.432
The tether's
over 300 kilometers long.

00:10:37.469 --> 00:10:39.403
It takes 12 hours
to reach the station.

00:10:39.437 --> 00:10:42.531
Well, we wouldn't have to go
all the way to the station.

00:10:42.574 --> 00:10:44.804
We just have to leave
the ionosphere.

00:10:44.843 --> 00:10:46.970
Once we get above
all this interference,

00:10:47.012 --> 00:10:49.003
we can contact Voyager...
they'll beam us aboard.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.638
I've already considered
that option.

00:10:50.682 --> 00:10:52.877
The carriage was damaged
on the last impact.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.579
The induction coils
are off-line.

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.819
Maybe we can replace the coils

00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:01.758
with attitude control thrusters
from the shuttle.

00:11:01.793 --> 00:11:03.954
It would take
a little creative mechanics,

00:11:04.062 --> 00:11:05.654
but I think we can do it.

00:11:05.697 --> 00:11:09.064
I spent two years on a tether
maintenance team on Rinax.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.568
The principles are undoubtedly
the same.

00:11:22.681 --> 00:11:23.978
Our probability
of being detected

00:11:24.015 --> 00:11:26.279
by Voyager
or the other rescue teams

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:28.149
is greatest if we remain here.

00:11:28.186 --> 00:11:29.710
What if they don't
find us in time?

00:11:29.754 --> 00:11:30.778
He's right.

00:11:30.822 --> 00:11:32.119
We should try the tether.

00:11:32.157 --> 00:11:34.955
It's better than sitting here
waiting to be buried in dust.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.397
I've helped rebuild
a dozen mag-lev carriages.

00:11:41.433 --> 00:11:43.765
Give me a chance
to get that one working.

00:11:43.802 --> 00:11:47.533
If I can't, we'll come back
and wait for the others.

00:11:52.477 --> 00:11:53.705
Very well.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.312
You won't regret this,
Lieutenant.

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:59.817
We need to get
to the base of the tether.

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.937
I think we can
integrate our thrusters

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.413
into the induction matrix,

00:12:30.448 --> 00:12:31.779
but we'll need to...

00:12:40.225 --> 00:12:42.420
Looks like
somebody's been here recently.

00:12:43.862 --> 00:12:45.090
Get away or I'll kill him!

00:12:53.338 --> 00:12:54.396
Drop your weapon!

00:12:54.439 --> 00:12:55.963
Now!

00:13:00.345 --> 00:13:02.040
This is my shelter.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.945
These are my supplies!

00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:05.914
We have no interest
in your supplies.

00:13:05.951 --> 00:13:08.511
We are here to use the carriage
to get to safety.

00:13:08.553 --> 00:13:09.952
He's telling the truth.

00:13:10.021 --> 00:13:11.955
We'll take you with us.

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:13.422
The carriage is damaged.

00:13:13.458 --> 00:13:15.187
Yes, we know.

00:13:15.226 --> 00:13:16.693
The induction coils.

00:13:16.728 --> 00:13:20.186
But we've brought equipment
to replace them.

00:13:20.231 --> 00:13:22.392
I know it's been difficult...

00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:25.198
this catastrophe has taken
it's toll on everyone...

00:13:25.236 --> 00:13:27.204
but you have got to believe us.

00:13:27.238 --> 00:13:29.365
We only want
to get off the surface.

00:13:29.407 --> 00:13:31.602
What-what about
the oxygen converters?

00:13:31.643 --> 00:13:33.201
They've been damaged, too.

00:13:33.244 --> 00:13:35.371
They can't produce
enough air for six people.

00:13:35.413 --> 00:13:36.971
Maybe we can augment
the converters.

00:13:37.048 --> 00:13:40.176
We brought along some equipment
that might do the trick.

00:13:44.155 --> 00:13:45.645
I don't have enough
rations for everyone.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.624
Don't expect me to share.

00:13:47.659 --> 00:13:52.494
If I can fix the tether,
no one will need your rations.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:54.794
We have a starship in orbit.

00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:57.768
They'll beam us aboard
once we leave the ionosphere.

00:14:12.183 --> 00:14:13.150
If I'm not mistaken,

00:14:13.184 --> 00:14:14.947
it sounds like
you know a thing or two

00:14:15.053 --> 00:14:16.213
about tethers, as well.

00:14:16.254 --> 00:14:17.721
Not really.

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:18.723
I'm a foundry worker.

00:14:18.757 --> 00:14:20.952
Good.

00:14:21.059 --> 00:14:23.459
We could use someone
with metallurgical knowledge.

00:14:25.563 --> 00:14:27.428
Let's get to work.

00:14:30.668 --> 00:14:32.465
Have faith, Mr. Vulcan.

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:34.563
We'll be tether-borne
in no time.

00:14:47.251 --> 00:14:49.742
I've completed
the mineralogical scans.

00:14:49.787 --> 00:14:53.382
The rock is composed
of tryoxene, olivine...

00:14:53.424 --> 00:14:55.415
Wait a minute.

00:14:55.459 --> 00:14:58.121
I'm reading
a concentration of triadium.

00:14:58.162 --> 00:14:59.288
Triadium?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.297
Isn't that an alloy?

00:15:00.331 --> 00:15:01.821
Yes.

00:15:01.866 --> 00:15:04.528
B'Elanna,
give me a hand with this.

00:15:10.842 --> 00:15:12.776
This doesn't look like
any asteroid I've ever seen.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.677
But I'll bet it's
the source of our triadium.

00:15:15.713 --> 00:15:17.544
It looks like a control node

00:15:17.582 --> 00:15:19.675
for some kind
of guidance system.

00:15:19.717 --> 00:15:20.945
Ambassador, I have a feeling

00:15:21.052 --> 00:15:23.612
these asteroids aren't striking
your planet by chance.

00:15:26.257 --> 00:15:28.623
Are we ready to bring
main power back on line?

00:15:28.659 --> 00:15:31.685
I... I think so.

00:15:32.864 --> 00:15:34.593
The coil bypass is active.

00:15:46.377 --> 00:15:48.538
Bypass is holding.

00:15:48.579 --> 00:15:50.706
Congratulations, Mr. Vulcan.

00:15:50.748 --> 00:15:51.976
We've done it!

00:15:52.049 --> 00:15:54.643
We must still repair
the oxygen regenerators

00:15:54.685 --> 00:15:56.380
and the damaged
tether couplings.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:57.853
Then let's get started.

00:15:57.889 --> 00:15:59.413
I'll go check
on the oxygen supply.

00:16:06.731 --> 00:16:08.699
How's it coming, Lillias?

00:16:08.733 --> 00:16:11.566
I still can't get
this power relay on line.

00:16:11.602 --> 00:16:13.160
I'm not an orbital engineer.

00:16:13.204 --> 00:16:14.171
I can't do this.

00:16:14.205 --> 00:16:16.105
Maybe I can help.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.334
Let's see.

00:16:20.378 --> 00:16:23.142
Aha.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:27.708
You need to recalibrate
the pressure valve...

00:16:27.752 --> 00:16:29.447
like this.

00:16:32.456 --> 00:16:33.582
That should about do it.

00:16:39.563 --> 00:16:41.963
We're going to need a name.

00:16:42.033 --> 00:16:43.591
A name?

00:16:43.634 --> 00:16:46.296
For the mag-lev carriage.

00:16:46.337 --> 00:16:50.364
Whenever we finished
building a tether on Rinax,

00:16:50.408 --> 00:16:52.376
we named the carriage
for good luck.

00:16:54.111 --> 00:16:55.669
Any suggestions?

00:16:57.682 --> 00:16:58.740
No.

00:17:00.084 --> 00:17:01.711
How about...

00:17:04.455 --> 00:17:06.286
Alixia?

00:17:06.324 --> 00:17:07.723
"Alixia"?

00:17:09.427 --> 00:17:10.894
My favorite sister.

00:17:10.928 --> 00:17:13.920
She was always
taking me out to explore.

00:17:14.031 --> 00:17:17.364
She showed me
the Caves of Touth...

00:17:17.401 --> 00:17:20.564
the equatorial dust shrouds.

00:17:20.604 --> 00:17:23.471
Once, she even took me
hunting for arctic spiders.

00:17:23.507 --> 00:17:28.137
Whenever I think of her,
I think of adventure.

00:17:28.179 --> 00:17:32.343
And this is an adventure
she would appreciate.

00:17:32.383 --> 00:17:34.476
What do you think?

00:17:34.518 --> 00:17:36.577
Where is your sister now?

00:17:38.522 --> 00:17:41.320
She was killed
when I was a young man

00:17:41.359 --> 00:17:42.951
in a war on my homeworld.

00:17:42.994 --> 00:17:44.689
My entire family was lost.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.195
I'm sorry.

00:17:47.231 --> 00:17:49.859
I still see each of them.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:53.961
Every night before I go to
sleep, I recall their faces

00:17:54.038 --> 00:17:56.734
and share something about my day
with each of them.

00:17:59.477 --> 00:18:01.877
Tonight, I'm going to have
quite a lot to tell them.

00:18:11.689 --> 00:18:13.020
Thank you.

00:18:19.463 --> 00:18:21.488
I have a sister, too.

00:18:21.532 --> 00:18:22.726
Halla.

00:18:22.767 --> 00:18:24.758
Three weeks ago,
after the first impact,

00:18:24.802 --> 00:18:29.102
our home was destroyed
and we were separated.

00:18:31.208 --> 00:18:32.766
I haven't seen her since.

00:18:36.647 --> 00:18:39.081
I don't even know
if she's alive.

00:18:39.116 --> 00:18:41.414
When we get back to Voyager,

00:18:41.452 --> 00:18:44.148
I'll ask my Captain
to help you find her.

00:18:44.188 --> 00:18:45.883
Mr. Neelix?

00:18:45.923 --> 00:18:47.413
Excuse me.

00:18:51.629 --> 00:18:52.789
Yes, sir!

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:56.027
Your interpersonal activities
are delaying our progress.

00:18:58.169 --> 00:18:59.227
What do you mean?

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:00.601
Since we arrived,

00:19:00.638 --> 00:19:03.106
you have spent as much time
engaged in idle conversation

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:05.108
as you have making repairs.

00:19:06.744 --> 00:19:09.144
I'm just trying to cheer
everyone up a little.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:10.704
Your function at the moment

00:19:10.748 --> 00:19:13.376
is to repair this vessel,
not to boost morale.

00:19:13.417 --> 00:19:17.012
This is not the holodeck,
nor the Mess Hall.

00:19:17.054 --> 00:19:18.453
This is a life-threatening
situation

00:19:18.489 --> 00:19:19.751
and your attention
should be focused

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:23.783
on one thing alone...
our safe return to Voyager.

00:19:25.529 --> 00:19:27.861
I'm sorry, sir.

00:19:27.898 --> 00:19:29.866
I'll finish as fast as I can.

00:19:39.577 --> 00:19:41.238
Once we start
moving up the tether,

00:19:41.278 --> 00:19:42.472
will we be able
to reverse course?

00:19:42.513 --> 00:19:44.208
It will take several hours
to reach the station.

00:19:44.248 --> 00:19:45.272
We've only been able

00:19:45.316 --> 00:19:46.943
to fix three of the
seven power supplies.

00:19:50.121 --> 00:19:51.315
...were to turn back,

00:19:51.355 --> 00:19:53.323
we might not be able
to break through the ionosphere.

00:19:53.357 --> 00:19:55.518
Mr. Sklar, examine this piece.

00:19:55.559 --> 00:19:57.550
See if the...

00:20:00.531 --> 00:20:02.260
Dr. Vatm!

00:20:02.299 --> 00:20:04.130
What are you doing?!

00:20:04.168 --> 00:20:05.795
He's opening the launch doors!

00:20:05.836 --> 00:20:07.428
- He's leaving without us!
- Dr. Vatm!

00:20:08.873 --> 00:20:10.340
Please stop!

00:20:12.476 --> 00:20:14.774
The tether's base
hasn't been secured!

00:20:14.812 --> 00:20:16.279
If he launches now,

00:20:16.313 --> 00:20:19.771
he'll destabilize
the entire cavern!

00:20:19.817 --> 00:20:21.785
Wait, please!

00:20:21.819 --> 00:20:23.286
Don't leave us here!

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.617
Stand aside.

00:20:35.299 --> 00:20:37.631
It's too late!

00:20:37.668 --> 00:20:39.636
The cavern support
structure is collapsing.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.728
We've got to get out of here.

00:20:40.771 --> 00:20:42.102
Can we launch?

00:20:42.139 --> 00:20:43.197
I think so.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.969
Seal that door.

00:20:45.009 --> 00:20:48.376
I despise enclosed spaces.

00:20:48.412 --> 00:20:49.572
Hang on.

00:21:05.562 --> 00:21:08.053
Velocity:
30 kilometers per hour.

00:21:08.098 --> 00:21:11.158
Internal atmospheric pressure:
700 millibars.

00:21:11.201 --> 00:21:12.828
Altitude: 800 meters
and climbing.

00:21:15.806 --> 00:21:17.706
We're losing mag-lev cohesion.

00:21:17.741 --> 00:21:18.708
All right.

00:21:18.742 --> 00:21:20.175
We have to stabilize
that right away.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.837
Otherwise, we'll go
into free fall.

00:21:21.878 --> 00:21:22.970
You mean, we're going to drop?

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.071
How do we prevent that?

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.081
- Neelix!
- Hold on! Hold on!

00:21:28.118 --> 00:21:29.016
I'm thinking!

00:21:31.088 --> 00:21:33.283
Velocity... let's try
increasing the velocity.

00:21:33.323 --> 00:21:34.585
It should stabilize
our ascent.

00:21:34.624 --> 00:21:37.058
See if you can increase power
to the tether couplings.

00:21:45.168 --> 00:21:47.693
Routing backup power
to the tether couplings.

00:21:47.737 --> 00:21:48.931
Stand by.

00:21:48.972 --> 00:21:51.133
I'm going to try giving her
a little more speed.

00:22:00.951 --> 00:22:05.650
Velocity:
47 kilometers per hour...

00:22:05.689 --> 00:22:07.213
and holding.

00:22:07.257 --> 00:22:09.054
Mag-lev cohesion...

00:22:09.092 --> 00:22:10.081
stable.

00:22:11.361 --> 00:22:12.885
We're all right.

00:22:12.929 --> 00:22:15.625
Good girl, Alixia.

00:22:15.665 --> 00:22:16.962
I knew you could do it.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.729
"Alixia"?

00:22:18.768 --> 00:22:21.396
I named the carriage
after my sister.

00:22:21.438 --> 00:22:23.963
For good luck, no doubt.

00:22:24.007 --> 00:22:25.440
We will need it.

00:22:25.475 --> 00:22:27.238
One of the oxygen converters
has ruptured.

00:22:28.245 --> 00:22:29.212
We'll have to find a way

00:22:29.246 --> 00:22:30.713
of increasing output
to the other converter.

00:22:30.747 --> 00:22:32.806
Otherwise, we'll run out of air
about halfway up.

00:22:32.849 --> 00:22:35.181
What are the chances
of our reaching the ionosphere?

00:22:35.218 --> 00:22:38.085
I'd say they, uh...
they were pretty good.

00:22:38.121 --> 00:22:39.850
We did leave ahead of schedule

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:42.256
and that could cause
a few glitches along the way.

00:22:43.827 --> 00:22:45.260
Glitches?

00:22:45.295 --> 00:22:47.160
I wasn't able to get
the auto-ascent sequencer

00:22:47.197 --> 00:22:48.164
back on line.

00:22:48.198 --> 00:22:49.165
That means, I'll have

00:22:49.199 --> 00:22:51.133
to keep controlling
the ascent manually.

00:22:51.168 --> 00:22:52.362
And there is the problem

00:22:52.402 --> 00:22:53.994
of maintaining
atmospheric pressure.

00:22:54.037 --> 00:22:56.699
I'm already beginning to detect
a few fissures in the hull.

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:58.298
We must repair them.

00:22:58.341 --> 00:23:00.673
Where is the emergency
containment grid?

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:01.335
Containment grid.

00:23:02.279 --> 00:23:04.747
Containment grid.

00:23:04.781 --> 00:23:05.873
Uh...

00:23:05.916 --> 00:23:06.974
I'm... I'm not quite sure.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.450
Mr. Neelix, you told
me you had experience

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:14.684
with this kind of technology.

00:23:14.724 --> 00:23:16.316
I did. I did.

00:23:16.359 --> 00:23:17.792
Sort of.

00:23:17.827 --> 00:23:19.556
They weren't exactly

00:23:19.596 --> 00:23:22.861
what you might call
working carriages.

00:23:22.899 --> 00:23:24.696
They were more like prototypes.

00:23:24.734 --> 00:23:26.167
Specifically.

00:23:26.203 --> 00:23:28.763
All right, they were models,
one-tenth scale,

00:23:28.805 --> 00:23:30.864
but they were
extremely detailed.

00:23:30.907 --> 00:23:32.397
You built models.

00:23:32.442 --> 00:23:33.966
Yes, but they were
basically identical

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.739
to real mag-lev carriages...

00:23:35.779 --> 00:23:37.974
same principles,
same mechanical components.

00:23:38.048 --> 00:23:40.141
I was planning
to familiarize myself

00:23:40.183 --> 00:23:41.912
with all the systems
on this carriage.

00:23:41.952 --> 00:23:44.147
I just didn't plan
on leaving ahead of schedule.

00:23:44.187 --> 00:23:46.712
But don't worry, I've got
everything under control.

00:23:48.325 --> 00:23:50.725
There is little we can
do now that we are

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.660
30 kilometers above the surface.

00:23:52.696 --> 00:23:53.788
I suggest we continue to...

00:23:53.830 --> 00:23:54.797
What are you doing?!

00:23:54.831 --> 00:23:56.423
Let's go.
You wanted to leave?

00:23:56.466 --> 00:23:58.434
Fine... then leave.

00:24:02.305 --> 00:24:03.932
That is enough.

00:24:06.776 --> 00:24:09.267
He may be crucial to the
survival of your colonies.

00:24:09.312 --> 00:24:11.041
He would've let us
die down there.

00:24:11.081 --> 00:24:13.481
That is no justification
for murder.

00:24:14.918 --> 00:24:18.752
Dr. Vatm, why did you try
to launch without us?

00:24:18.788 --> 00:24:21.086
Does it have to do
with the discovery you made

00:24:21.124 --> 00:24:22.386
about the asteroids?

00:24:22.425 --> 00:24:26.293
Answer him, or I'll
throw you out myself.

00:24:26.329 --> 00:24:28.229
Compose yourself, Mr. Hanjuan.

00:24:28.265 --> 00:24:30.199
Once we return to Voyager,
we will find out...

00:24:30.233 --> 00:24:31.860
Who put you in command?

00:24:31.901 --> 00:24:33.562
This rescue mission
was authorized

00:24:33.603 --> 00:24:34.900
by the Captain of my ship

00:24:34.938 --> 00:24:36.803
and the ambassador
of your government.

00:24:36.840 --> 00:24:38.467
I say we throw Vatm
out the door.

00:24:38.508 --> 00:24:40.408
We could use the extra oxygen.

00:24:40.443 --> 00:24:42.604
If you are trying
to intimidate me,

00:24:42.646 --> 00:24:44.614
I should inform you
that, as a Vulcan,

00:24:44.648 --> 00:24:46.548
I possess physical strength
many times your...

00:24:52.489 --> 00:24:55.583
It is going to be a long
and perilous journey.

00:24:55.625 --> 00:24:58.958
As such, I will need
your full cooperation.

00:24:58.995 --> 00:25:00.292
Understood?

00:25:00.330 --> 00:25:01.763
Yeah.

00:25:10.473 --> 00:25:13.135
Mechanical glitches
would seem to be

00:25:13.176 --> 00:25:15.167
the least of our problems.

00:25:18.114 --> 00:25:21.083
We've just completed
our third low-altitude survey.

00:25:21.117 --> 00:25:24.780
There's no sign of Dr. Vatm
or Tuvok and his rescue team.

00:25:24.821 --> 00:25:26.948
We're monitoring
a major dust storm

00:25:27.057 --> 00:25:28.319
heading your way.

00:25:28.358 --> 00:25:30.326
You'll need to head due north
within the hour.

00:25:30.360 --> 00:25:31.884
Acknowledged.
Paris out.

00:25:31.928 --> 00:25:34.260
Captain, I'm getting more
detailed sensor readings

00:25:34.297 --> 00:25:35.628
on the approaching asteroid.

00:25:35.665 --> 00:25:38.293
It's huge... over half
a kilometer in diameter...

00:25:38.335 --> 00:25:40.132
and it's moving faster
than the others.

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:41.501
Time to impact?

00:25:42.672 --> 00:25:44.765
Approximately two hours.

00:26:13.136 --> 00:26:17.732
Doctor, I'm going to inject you
with a triox compound.

00:26:17.774 --> 00:26:19.969
It will help
to oxygenate your blood.

00:26:33.056 --> 00:26:35.251
I've prepared an injection of...

00:26:35.291 --> 00:26:37.350
Yes, uh, I know.

00:26:37.394 --> 00:26:38.361
I heard you.

00:26:38.395 --> 00:26:41.296
It...

00:26:41.331 --> 00:26:43.424
won't be painful, will it?

00:26:43.466 --> 00:26:46.594
No. It is a simple
subdermal transfer.

00:26:46.636 --> 00:26:48.604
Oh, good. Good.

00:26:48.638 --> 00:26:50.230
I... I despise needles.

00:26:53.943 --> 00:26:56.241
Any progress with the...

00:26:56.279 --> 00:26:58.179
with the converters?

00:26:58.214 --> 00:27:00.774
We were unable to salvage
the damaged tank.

00:27:00.817 --> 00:27:01.909
But Lillias is working

00:27:01.951 --> 00:27:04.317
to increase the efficiency
of the functioning one.

00:27:04.354 --> 00:27:07.790
And if she can't,
we'll all suffocate.

00:27:07.824 --> 00:27:09.189
It is illogical

00:27:09.225 --> 00:27:11.750
to dwell on situations
beyond your control.

00:27:11.795 --> 00:27:14.195
It will only serve
to heighten your anxiety,

00:27:14.230 --> 00:27:17.028
which, if I may say so,
is heightened enough.

00:27:17.066 --> 00:27:21.059
Oh. Well, thank you
for the reassurance.

00:27:27.343 --> 00:27:29.538
How is everybody?

00:27:29.579 --> 00:27:30.944
They are suffering
the initial stages

00:27:31.014 --> 00:27:33.278
of carbon dioxide poisoning.

00:27:33.316 --> 00:27:34.544
And you?

00:27:34.584 --> 00:27:37.144
My lungs are capable
of respirating

00:27:37.187 --> 00:27:39.655
in an extremely thin atmosphere.

00:27:41.424 --> 00:27:43.221
Then if we can't fix
this air supply,

00:27:43.259 --> 00:27:46.092
you may be the only one left
to pilot this thing.

00:27:46.129 --> 00:27:49.428
I'd better start showing you
how to use the ascent thrusters.

00:27:52.969 --> 00:27:56.268
They must be kept
at a minimum temperature...

00:27:56.306 --> 00:27:57.273
Stop!
What are you doing?

00:27:57.307 --> 00:27:58.296
Get away.

00:27:59.476 --> 00:28:01.307
I've got to get out.

00:28:01.344 --> 00:28:02.242
Let me out.

00:28:02.278 --> 00:28:04.542
Let go of me.

00:28:04.581 --> 00:28:05.912
I need it.

00:28:05.982 --> 00:28:07.677
So, now he wants to leave.

00:28:07.717 --> 00:28:08.684
Let him.

00:28:08.718 --> 00:28:10.379
No, you don't understand.

00:28:10.420 --> 00:28:11.887
There's something out there.

00:28:11.921 --> 00:28:13.252
What is out there?

00:28:13.289 --> 00:28:14.688
On...

00:28:14.724 --> 00:28:16.658
the roof.

00:28:18.862 --> 00:28:20.022
He's going into shock.

00:28:28.838 --> 00:28:30.271
He's dead.

00:28:31.741 --> 00:28:33.368
Can you revive him?

00:28:34.577 --> 00:28:37.137
His cardiopulmonary tissues
have begun to deteriorate.

00:28:37.180 --> 00:28:39.114
From lack of oxygen?

00:28:39.148 --> 00:28:40.638
No.

00:28:43.953 --> 00:28:46.114
I believe he was murdered.

00:28:57.300 --> 00:28:59.097
Murdered? How?

00:28:59.135 --> 00:29:00.124
Poisoning.

00:29:02.272 --> 00:29:04.240
According
to my tricorder readings,

00:29:04.274 --> 00:29:05.468
his water supply has been

00:29:05.508 --> 00:29:07.738
contaminated
with a lydroxide corrosive.

00:29:07.777 --> 00:29:09.369
Lydroxide?

00:29:09.412 --> 00:29:11.812
That's the coolant used
in the tether couplings.

00:29:11.848 --> 00:29:13.509
How do you know
it wasn't an accident?

00:29:13.550 --> 00:29:16.041
The coolant system
is completely sealed.

00:29:16.085 --> 00:29:18.553
And there is no lydroxide
anywhere else on board.

00:29:18.588 --> 00:29:21.148
Now we have a choice between
death by suffocation

00:29:21.191 --> 00:29:23.318
or death by poisoning.

00:29:23.359 --> 00:29:26.851
I will conduct an investigation
once we return to the ship.

00:29:26.896 --> 00:29:29.524
For now, we must focus
on survival.

00:29:29.566 --> 00:29:31.466
Again, you take command.

00:29:31.501 --> 00:29:33.594
Again, you decide our fate.

00:29:33.636 --> 00:29:35.365
How do we know you
didn't kill him?

00:29:35.405 --> 00:29:37.373
I have no motive.

00:29:37.407 --> 00:29:40.774
Your motive would be
the same as ours... revenge.

00:29:40.810 --> 00:29:42.209
I am Vulcan.

00:29:42.245 --> 00:29:43.803
I do not succumb to emotion.

00:29:43.847 --> 00:29:45.940
Oh, and we are expected
to believe that.

00:29:45.982 --> 00:29:47.347
I think we should stop
the carriage.

00:29:47.383 --> 00:29:48.350
Why?

00:29:48.384 --> 00:29:51.444
Something Dr. Vatm said...

00:29:51.488 --> 00:29:53.353
about getting up on the roof.

00:29:53.389 --> 00:29:56.517
Dr. Vatm was delirious
from lack of oxygen.

00:29:56.559 --> 00:29:58.550
He attempted to open
the hatch of this vessel

00:29:58.595 --> 00:29:59.653
and go outside.

00:29:59.696 --> 00:30:02.062
It would have killed him
and possibly all of us as well.

00:30:02.098 --> 00:30:04.862
Exactly. He was desperate enough
to risk his own life.

00:30:04.901 --> 00:30:07.529
I think we should go up and find
out what he was talking about.

00:30:07.570 --> 00:30:09.868
If we stop the carriage,

00:30:09.906 --> 00:30:12.067
we'll risk losing
mag-lev cohesion again.

00:30:12.108 --> 00:30:14.235
We'll check the roof
upon returning to Voyager.

00:30:14.277 --> 00:30:15.574
I don't know.

00:30:15.612 --> 00:30:18.274
I've got a funny feeling
about this.

00:30:18.314 --> 00:30:20.714
I'm not interested
in your funny feeling.

00:30:20.750 --> 00:30:23.184
You're not listening
to what I'm saying.

00:30:23.219 --> 00:30:24.243
Delirious or not,

00:30:24.287 --> 00:30:26.881
he said he needed
whatever's up there.

00:30:26.923 --> 00:30:28.788
What if it's something
that can help us?

00:30:28.825 --> 00:30:30.292
I will not debate this with you.

00:30:30.326 --> 00:30:32.089
Please pilot the craft
and remain silent.

00:30:32.128 --> 00:30:34.187
You're going to listen to me!

00:30:39.302 --> 00:30:41.463
You are becoming
emotionally distraught.

00:30:41.504 --> 00:30:43.972
There is little point
in furthering this discussion.

00:30:44.007 --> 00:30:46.237
I'll tell you
who's being emotional... you.

00:30:46.276 --> 00:30:48.107
You hide it
beneath that Vulcan calm,

00:30:48.144 --> 00:30:50.442
but the truth is, you're filled
with contempt and sarcasm

00:30:50.480 --> 00:30:52.971
and I'm tired of being the
target of all your hostility.

00:30:53.016 --> 00:30:54.483
You are mistaken.

00:30:54.517 --> 00:30:55.745
No, he's not.

00:30:55.785 --> 00:30:58.185
I can see it every time
you talk to Neelix.

00:30:58.221 --> 00:31:00.155
You're dismissive
and condescending.

00:31:00.189 --> 00:31:02.783
You are projecting your own
emotional bias onto my actions.

00:31:02.825 --> 00:31:04.588
I have no feelings
toward Mr. Neelix.

00:31:04.627 --> 00:31:05.594
That's right!

00:31:05.628 --> 00:31:07.220
That's exactly
what I'm talking about!

00:31:07.263 --> 00:31:08.855
You have no feelings for me,

00:31:08.898 --> 00:31:11.298
but you have feelings
against me.

00:31:11.334 --> 00:31:13.325
For three years,
you've ridiculed me

00:31:13.369 --> 00:31:16.099
and made it obvious to everyone
that you have no respect for me

00:31:16.139 --> 00:31:18.130
and I've tolerated it.

00:31:18.174 --> 00:31:20.142
You know why?
You know why?

00:31:20.176 --> 00:31:22.667
Because you are smarter
than I am, Tuvok,

00:31:22.712 --> 00:31:26.148
and more logical, and...
stronger

00:31:26.182 --> 00:31:28.673
and superior
in almost every way.

00:31:28.718 --> 00:31:30.743
And I admire you,

00:31:30.787 --> 00:31:33.119
but you don't have
any instincts.

00:31:33.156 --> 00:31:34.987
You don't have any gut feelings

00:31:35.058 --> 00:31:38.516
and you don't really
understand people.

00:31:38.561 --> 00:31:41.121
But non-Vulcans have feelings
and they have to listen to them.

00:31:41.164 --> 00:31:42.961
And I've got to listen to mine,

00:31:42.999 --> 00:31:44.432
and right now,
they're telling me

00:31:44.467 --> 00:31:45.798
we need to get up on that roof

00:31:45.835 --> 00:31:47.666
and find out what the Doctor
was talking about.

00:31:49.072 --> 00:31:50.801
I disagree.

00:31:50.840 --> 00:31:52.102
Fine!

00:31:54.911 --> 00:31:57.573
But I'm the only one
who can pilot this vessel

00:31:57.614 --> 00:32:00.105
and we're not going anywhere

00:32:00.149 --> 00:32:02.447
till someone
goes up on that roof.

00:32:09.525 --> 00:32:11.652
You leave me little choice.

00:32:14.163 --> 00:32:15.824
All right, then...

00:32:15.865 --> 00:32:19.892
now... one of us
needs to go outside.

00:32:19.936 --> 00:32:21.767
I'm not going out there.

00:32:21.804 --> 00:32:23.965
Don't even think about me.

00:32:24.073 --> 00:32:25.836
I'm willing to give it...

00:32:25.875 --> 00:32:27.342
I will go.

00:32:27.377 --> 00:32:28.366
You?

00:32:28.411 --> 00:32:30.971
I am the logical one
to make the egress.

00:32:31.014 --> 00:32:33.482
I can breathe
the rarefied atmosphere.

00:32:37.587 --> 00:32:39.179
I can't believe
you're going out there.

00:32:39.222 --> 00:32:40.519
You don't even know
what you're looking for.

00:32:40.556 --> 00:32:43.252
I am looking for
Mr. Neelix's instinct.

00:32:43.292 --> 00:32:45.590
Perhaps it will be marked.

00:32:56.506 --> 00:32:58.235
It's strange...

00:32:58.274 --> 00:33:00.401
but I really like him.

00:33:03.246 --> 00:33:05.271
I just wish the feeling
were mutual.

00:33:43.419 --> 00:33:44.909
Tuvok to Neelix.

00:33:44.954 --> 00:33:46.512
Go ahead.

00:33:46.556 --> 00:33:48.421
I have found
a data storage device

00:33:48.458 --> 00:33:50.756
lodged in the internal
circuitry.

00:33:50.793 --> 00:33:52.954
It appears
to contain information

00:33:52.995 --> 00:33:55.555
about an alien starship.

00:33:55.598 --> 00:33:56.724
But I will need to remove it

00:33:56.766 --> 00:33:58.927
and bring it into the cabin
for further examination.

00:33:58.968 --> 00:34:00.492
Be careful up there.

00:34:00.536 --> 00:34:02.663
If you can't remove it, don't.

00:34:04.807 --> 00:34:05.774
Sklar!

00:34:05.808 --> 00:34:07.332
What are you doing?!

00:34:13.149 --> 00:34:15.379
Neelix!

00:34:57.926 --> 00:34:59.553
Where's Tuvok?

00:34:59.595 --> 00:35:03.053
Mr. Tuvok returned
to the surface.

00:35:06.668 --> 00:35:08.192
Get this carriage moving.

00:35:08.237 --> 00:35:09.329
What are you?

00:35:09.371 --> 00:35:10.429
Now!

00:35:10.472 --> 00:35:12.372
He can't.
He's hurt.

00:35:12.407 --> 00:35:14.375
Back away.

00:35:19.081 --> 00:35:20.275
Get up.

00:35:25.053 --> 00:35:27.112
Get up!

00:35:30.626 --> 00:35:32.526
Well...

00:35:32.561 --> 00:35:34.188
we're going
to have to figure out

00:35:34.229 --> 00:35:35.423
how to fly this vessel.

00:35:39.935 --> 00:35:41.800
Captain, the asteroid
is within visual range.

00:35:41.837 --> 00:35:43.099
Let's see it.

00:35:44.573 --> 00:35:45.597
Ensign.

00:35:45.641 --> 00:35:49.771
There's a large crew
complement... at least 2,000.

00:35:49.811 --> 00:35:52.302
They remodulated their shields
to fool our sensors.

00:35:52.347 --> 00:35:54.577
We're being hailed.

00:35:54.616 --> 00:35:55.742
On screen.

00:35:55.784 --> 00:35:59.686
The Etanian Order
claims this territory.

00:35:59.721 --> 00:36:01.848
You will withdraw.

00:36:01.890 --> 00:36:03.790
This planet belongs to the Nezu.

00:36:03.825 --> 00:36:05.656
They have five colonies here.

00:36:05.694 --> 00:36:07.525
You are not Nezu.

00:36:07.563 --> 00:36:09.087
I'm a friend of theirs,

00:36:09.131 --> 00:36:11.065
Kathryn Janeway,
and I'm not going anywhere

00:36:11.099 --> 00:36:13.294
until you've lowered
your weapons.

00:36:13.335 --> 00:36:15.326
You will be willing to die
for them?

00:36:15.370 --> 00:36:18.203
A loyal friend

00:36:18.240 --> 00:36:20.299
and a foolish one.

00:36:21.143 --> 00:36:22.110
They'll be here

00:36:22.144 --> 00:36:23.304
in under ten minutes, Captain.

00:36:29.051 --> 00:36:31.451
Battle stations.

00:36:35.924 --> 00:36:37.050
Why haven't we started?

00:36:37.092 --> 00:36:38.320
If we don't get moving soon,

00:36:38.360 --> 00:36:39.554
the tether couplings
will give out.

00:36:39.595 --> 00:36:40.653
They'll snap.

00:36:40.696 --> 00:36:42.288
We'll lose mag-lev cohesion.

00:36:42.331 --> 00:36:43.423
Then get us moving.

00:36:43.465 --> 00:36:45.296
I can't!
I don't know how.

00:36:45.334 --> 00:36:47.734
There's the accelerator control.
Try it.

00:36:47.769 --> 00:36:48.736
Too dangerous.

00:36:48.770 --> 00:36:50.761
We've got to secure
the tether first.

00:36:50.806 --> 00:36:53.502
All right, you, go outside

00:36:53.542 --> 00:36:54.509
and check the couplings.

00:36:54.543 --> 00:36:55.805
Make sure
they haven't given out.

00:36:55.844 --> 00:36:56.970
I'm not going out there.

00:36:57.045 --> 00:36:58.569
Besides, I wouldn't know
what to look for.

00:36:58.614 --> 00:37:00.172
The only person
who knows how to pilot

00:37:00.215 --> 00:37:02.683
this ship is Neelix.

00:37:02.718 --> 00:37:05.346
It can't be that complicated!

00:37:05.387 --> 00:37:06.581
Keep trying.

00:37:06.622 --> 00:37:09.352
I'm doing my best.

00:37:13.161 --> 00:37:14.560
Come on, come on, come on.

00:38:23.999 --> 00:38:25.728
I'm glad you're all right.

00:38:25.767 --> 00:38:28.167
Fortunately,
I was able to grab hold

00:38:28.203 --> 00:38:30.603
of an induction coil
and climb to safety.

00:38:33.508 --> 00:38:35.305
Thank you, Mr. Neelix.

00:38:37.746 --> 00:38:38.770
What?

00:38:38.814 --> 00:38:43.012
I said thank you
for opening the door.

00:38:44.920 --> 00:38:46.251
Don't mention it.

00:38:46.288 --> 00:38:49.689
I believe
we know now who killed Dr. Vatm.

00:38:49.725 --> 00:38:50.919
But why did he kill him?

00:38:50.959 --> 00:38:52.620
The data storage device contains

00:38:52.661 --> 00:38:54.925
tactical information
about an alien starship...

00:38:54.963 --> 00:38:57.955
weapons, warp drive,
shield modulations.

00:38:58.066 --> 00:39:00.796
Apparently, Sklar
did not want us to find it.

00:39:04.773 --> 00:39:07.105
You have
an occipital concussion.

00:39:07.142 --> 00:39:11.135
I'm afraid my understanding of
Talaxian physiology is limited.

00:39:11.179 --> 00:39:13.170
I cannot treat you.

00:39:15.417 --> 00:39:17.009
I don't know how to do this.

00:39:17.052 --> 00:39:20.021
We're going to lose cohesion
any minute now.

00:39:20.055 --> 00:39:21.716
Neelix.

00:39:21.757 --> 00:39:23.315
We need you.

00:39:26.395 --> 00:39:28.295
I don't think I can do it.

00:39:28.330 --> 00:39:30.059
You must.

00:39:30.098 --> 00:39:32.692
I can barely keep my eyes open.

00:39:40.642 --> 00:39:42.667
Do it...

00:39:42.711 --> 00:39:44.178
for Alixia.

00:39:46.848 --> 00:39:49.112
She would be proud of you.

00:39:53.021 --> 00:39:53.953
I'm glad to see

00:39:54.022 --> 00:39:56.422
your interpersonal
skills are improving.

00:40:05.033 --> 00:40:07.024
You're learning
how to motivate people.

00:40:19.114 --> 00:40:22.106
Speed: 45 kilometers per hour.

00:40:25.620 --> 00:40:27.451
The ship is within range.

00:40:27.489 --> 00:40:28.956
They're charging weapons.

00:40:28.990 --> 00:40:31.049
Full power to the shields.
Ready phasers.

00:40:32.727 --> 00:40:34.456
Shields down to 85 percent!

00:40:34.496 --> 00:40:35.895
Return fire.

00:40:35.930 --> 00:40:37.659
No effect.

00:40:37.699 --> 00:40:39.291
We can't penetrate
their shields.

00:40:40.335 --> 00:40:42.303
Hang on!

00:40:42.337 --> 00:40:45.067
We're breaking through
the ionosphere!

00:40:50.879 --> 00:40:53.211
Engaging induction dampers.

00:40:58.486 --> 00:40:59.817
We did it.

00:41:00.955 --> 00:41:02.513
We made it.

00:41:08.830 --> 00:41:10.297
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:41:10.331 --> 00:41:11.298
Janeway here.

00:41:11.332 --> 00:41:12.594
Are you all right, Lieutenant?

00:41:12.634 --> 00:41:14.499
Yes, Captain.

00:41:14.536 --> 00:41:15.901
We're a little busy right now.

00:41:15.937 --> 00:41:17.427
Prepare to beam aboard.

00:41:22.510 --> 00:41:23.909
Shields down to 23 percent.

00:41:23.945 --> 00:41:25.640
Structural integrity is failing.

00:41:25.680 --> 00:41:27.807
Captain.

00:41:27.849 --> 00:41:30.579
This data device contains
tactical information

00:41:30.618 --> 00:41:31.607
about the enemy vessel,

00:41:31.653 --> 00:41:33.644
including
their shield modulation.

00:41:34.923 --> 00:41:36.788
Adjust our phasers to match.

00:41:36.824 --> 00:41:38.917
Target their primary reactor.

00:41:39.961 --> 00:41:41.258
Ready.

00:41:41.296 --> 00:41:42.854
Fire at will.

00:41:46.701 --> 00:41:47.929
Direct hit.

00:41:47.969 --> 00:41:49.334
Their reactor is off-line.

00:41:50.371 --> 00:41:53.272
They're remodulating
their shields.

00:41:53.308 --> 00:41:54.935
Target their weapons array.

00:41:54.976 --> 00:41:56.136
Fire.

00:42:00.148 --> 00:42:01.445
Their weapons
have been destroyed.

00:42:02.784 --> 00:42:04.308
They're retreating, Captain.

00:42:09.591 --> 00:42:11.957
What happened to you down there?

00:42:11.993 --> 00:42:13.620
Where's Sklar?

00:42:13.661 --> 00:42:15.060
Mr. Sklar...

00:42:18.433 --> 00:42:20.594
returned to the surface.

00:42:29.444 --> 00:42:31.969
I've just come
from a staff briefing.

00:42:36.584 --> 00:42:39.485
The people who attacked
your colonies,

00:42:39.520 --> 00:42:41.988
they call themselves
the Etanian Order.

00:42:42.023 --> 00:42:43.513
Apparently,
they have a unique way

00:42:43.558 --> 00:42:45.526
of invading other worlds.

00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:46.959
First, they create

00:42:46.995 --> 00:42:49.623
what appears to be
a natural disaster...

00:42:49.664 --> 00:42:52.326
in your case,
an asteroid bombardment.

00:42:52.367 --> 00:42:54.665
Once the population
has evacuated,

00:42:54.702 --> 00:42:56.897
they arrive
and stake their claim.

00:42:56.938 --> 00:42:59.702
But they didn't expect
Voyager to intervene,

00:42:59.741 --> 00:43:02.904
so they arrived before our
colonies had been evacuated.

00:43:02.944 --> 00:43:03.774
Exactly.

00:43:03.811 --> 00:43:05.574
What about Dr. Vatm?

00:43:05.613 --> 00:43:06.739
From what we could tell,

00:43:06.781 --> 00:43:09.341
Dr. Vatm found out
about the Etanian Order

00:43:09.384 --> 00:43:11.318
and was secretly
collecting information

00:43:11.352 --> 00:43:12.842
about their starship technology.

00:43:12.887 --> 00:43:15.447
He also knew
that one of your colonists

00:43:15.490 --> 00:43:17.583
was a traitor,
helping the Etanians,

00:43:17.625 --> 00:43:20.526
feeding your government false
information about the asteroids.

00:43:20.561 --> 00:43:23.553
But he didn't know
that it was Sklar.

00:43:23.598 --> 00:43:25.293
He didn't know who to trust.

00:43:25.333 --> 00:43:29.030
That's why he tried to hide the
data storage device on the roof.

00:43:33.775 --> 00:43:36.573
The damage to our world
could have been much worse.

00:43:38.913 --> 00:43:40.278
Thank you.

00:43:46.721 --> 00:43:49.417
I have just received word
from the ambassador.

00:43:49.457 --> 00:43:51.118
Your sister, Halla,
has been found.

00:43:52.193 --> 00:43:54.423
Tell her I said hello.

00:44:00.301 --> 00:44:02.326
Mr. Neelix.

00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:04.270
I thought you should know
that I have submitted

00:44:04.305 --> 00:44:05.932
my mission report
to the Captain.

00:44:06.040 --> 00:44:07.940
I have given you
a special commendation

00:44:08.009 --> 00:44:09.135
for your endurance

00:44:09.177 --> 00:44:11.077
and bravery.

00:44:11.112 --> 00:44:13.672
I'm honored.

00:44:13.715 --> 00:44:16.741
Your instincts were correct.

00:44:16.784 --> 00:44:20.515
However, one day
your intuition will fail,

00:44:20.555 --> 00:44:22.182
and you will finally understand

00:44:22.223 --> 00:44:24.851
that logic is primary
above all else.

00:44:24.892 --> 00:44:28.350
Instinct is simply another term
for "serendipity."

00:44:28.396 --> 00:44:32.765
And one day, Mr. Vulcan,
I'll get you to trust your gut.

00:44:32.800 --> 00:44:34.427
That is doubtful.

00:44:34.469 --> 00:44:35.936
We'll see.

00:44:35.970 --> 00:44:38.438
Your attempts
have yet to succeed.

00:44:38.473 --> 00:44:42.534
You always have to get in
that last word, don't you?

00:44:42.577 --> 00:44:45.546
I am simply responding
to your erroneous statement.

00:44:45.580 --> 00:44:46.979
Something tells me

00:44:47.048 --> 00:44:49.778
you just hate
to lose an argument.

00:44:49.817 --> 00:44:52.012
Losing is irrelevant.

00:44:53.121 --> 00:44:54.179
See what I mean?

00:44:54.222 --> 00:44:57.953
No. I do not.
